Collision uses `prevY`, but after platform x movement, fine.

Cat trail: push position every frame if playing; limit 8; decay.

`updatePlaying(dt)`:
- runTime.
- steering from pointer/keys.
- P.blink.
- gravity, x movement, clamp.
- moving platforms x update; bounce decay; fragile timers.
- collision.
- camera.
- progress, sector.
- generate/prune.
- shards: magnet and collect.
- orbs: update x and collision.
- invuln.
- fall.
- win via progress >= GOAL.
- HUD update.
- ambient particles maybe.

Note: triggerWin sets state 'won' inside update; after that the rest of updatePlaying continues? Should return after trigger. Add checks.

`hurt` sets state; updatePlaying should return.

Camera during playing: 
```
const target = P.y - H*0.62;
if (target < game.camY) game.camY = lerp(game.camY, target, 1-Math.exp(-dt*8));
```
If player is falling, camera stays. Good.

But the start camera was P.y - H*0.62 where P.y ~ -23 → -581, screen feet at? (0-(-581)) = 581, 65%. Good.

Shards collection: magnet within 92, move toward player at 160*dt. Collect if dist<32.
On collect: got; shardsGot++; sound.shard; burst; float text "+1"; ring small. Note float text uses pal accent.

Orbs: x = baseX + sin(time*speed+phase)*amp; spin. Collision distance < o.r + 16 and invuln<=0. Need y visible.

Falling death threshold: game.camY + H + 180.

Sector: if maxProgress crosses multiple thresholds, set directly to floor/1000 (skip intermediate if huge boost unlikely). `const s=Math.min(8,Math.floor(game.maxProgress/1000)); if(s!==game.sector) setSectorVisuals(s,false);` But on retry sector resets 0. Good.

Win: `if(game.progress >= GOAL - 1) triggerWin()` — progress feet. But can progress be exactly GOAL in air above summit? yes. Trigger. Require summitPlaced to avoid weird. Use >= GOAL - 0.5.

`triggerWin`:
```
if state!=='playing' return;
state='won'; pendingWin=true; overlayTimer=1.5; sound.win; flash white; best update? at presentEnd.
P.vy=-JUMP*0.55; P.invuln=999;
burst x... confetti 100; rings;
showBanner('9000 M','SUMMIT');
```
Hide hint toast.

`hurt`:
```
if state!=='playing'||P.invuln>0 return;
game.lives--; updateHearts();
sound.hurt(); flash red; shake 16;
burst(...); floatText(P.x, P.y-30, '-1 LIFE', [255,95,120], 18);
if lives<=0 { state='dead'; overlayTimer=1.25; pendingWin=false; sound.over(); P.invuln=999; P.vy=-500; big burst; return; }
respawn();
```
Respawn after 0? Immediate. Add `P.invuln=2`.

Respawn camera snap might move camera down; that's fine but progress stays.

```
function respawn(){
 const safe=game.lastSafe;
 let x=view.worldW/2, y=0;
 if(safe){
   if(safe.platform && !safe.platform.dead){x=safe.platform.x;y=safe.platform.y}
   else if(safe.x!=null){x=safe.x;y=safe.y}
 }
 P.x=clamp(x,...); P.y=y-PLAYER.h/2-2; P.vx=0; P.vy=-JUMP*0.85; P.invuln=2;
 game.camY=P.y-H*0.62;
 ring...
}
```
Wait lastSafe stored {platform}. For start platform yes. Use `safe.platform.x`.

But camera snap when respawning at start (y=0) from high up (progress 3000) would snap down drastically and undo view — intended loss? Player's progress max remains but they restart at start, then climb... too punishing. lastSafe is the last platform landed, so at death by hazard near high progress, lastSafe is recent. Good. Fall deaths also recent. So fine. If lastSafe got pruned? If player is falling far, camera doesn't follow down, so platform stays on screen? lastSafe could be above camera? Wait lastSafe is above (since player fell below). Not pruned because pruning below camera + 480. Fine.

But after respawn camera moves to safe, showing area. Good.

Add slight camera smoothing? Snap fine.

Menu update: animate blink, bob, occasional particles. Cat idle uses `P.y`; update blink. Also make shards spin via time only. Add ambient floating motes around camera:
```
if(Math.random()<dt*3) addParticle(rand(0,worldW), camY+rand(0,H), {vx:rand(-10,10),vy:rand(-30,-8),life:rand(2,4),size:rand(1,3),color:pal.accent,grav:0,type:'mote'});
```
Add particle type mote with low alpha.

Effects update:
```
for parts: p.life-=dt; p.vy+=grav*dt; p.x+=vx*dt; p.y+=vy*dt; vx*=drag; vy*=drag? use pow; 
rings: r += (maxR-r)*dt*6; life-=dt
texts: y-=30*dt; life-=dt
flash decay exp
shake random
```
But shake random computed each update. Use `game.shakeX = (Math.random()*2-1)*game.shake` if !reducedMotion else 0.

Particles ambient in menu update.

End update:
```
function updateEnd(dt){
 if(game.overlayTimer>0){game.overlayTimer-=dt; if(game.overlayTimer<=0){presentEnd(game.pendingWin);}}
}
```
Need ensure presentEnd only once: set overlayTimer=0.

Main loop:
```
let last=performance.now();
function loop(now){
 const dt=Math.min((now-last)/1000,0.05); last=now;
 update(dt);
 render();
 requestAnimationFrame(loop);
}
```
Update paused: still palette? no. Render static.

Also `game.time` used for animations; pause stops. Fine.

`update(dt)`:
```
if(game.state==='paused') { return; }
game.time += dt;
updatePalette(dt);
sound.update();
updateEffects(dt);
if(game.state==='menu') updateMenu(dt);
else if(game.state==='playing') updatePlaying(dt);
else if(game.state==='dead'||game.state==='won') updateEnd(dt);
```
Note updateEffects before state update means new particles update next frame; fine.

Shake decay in updateEffects. Also `game.flash *= exp(-dt*5)`.

In ended states, cat stays.

`showScoreFloat` unused; remove? dom.scoreFloat unused but harmless.

